1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Abaqa Khan (1234–1282), also Abaga (Mongolian: Абага, “paternal uncle”), Abaka or Abagha Khan, was the second Mongol ruler (Il-khan) of the Persian Ilkhanate. The son of Hulagu Khan and Yesuncin Khatun,[1] he reign
2 CONC ed from 1265–1282. He settled in Tabriz - 1234-1282
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abaqa
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT *http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abaqa_Khan
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MONGOLS.htm#Abagadied1282
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Protector of Christians 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.academia.edu/788646/_A_Mongol_Princess_Making_Hajj_the_Biography_of_El_Qutlugh_Daughter_of_Abagha_Ilkhan_r._1265-82_Journal_of_Royal_Asiatic_Society_JRAS_21_3_2011_pp._331-359
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of Hulagu Khan and Yesuncin Khatun His vizir is Nezam ud din
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a great devotee of Sheikh Sa'adi Shirazi and Jalaludin Rumi and would often attend them. His son Naqudar Aghlan succeded him http://bit.ly/1RiJ7N8
2 CONT
2 CONT ABAQA (Mongolia 1234-Hamadan 1 Apr 1282).  Governor of Khorasan and Mazandaran.  He succeeded his father in 1265 as ABAQA Il-Khan, through the influence of his mother and was enthroned at Tuzlu Gol 19 Jun 1265 and again at Jaghatu
2 CONC  18 Nov 1270 on receipt of confirmation from the Great Khan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/abaqa
2 CONT
2 CONT Abaqa died at Hamadan on 1 April 1282, probably in a state of delirium tremens. This illness was probably caused by too much consumption of alcohol, a habit common to many Mongol leaders. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was buried, like his father, on the island of Šāhī in Lake Reżāʾīya. Both his two sons, Arḡun and Gaiḵatu (q.v.), were later to ascend the throne in turn, but his immediate successor was his brother Tegüder, who had adopted Isl
2 CONC am and assumed the name of Aḥmad (see Aḥmad Tegüder).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Governor of Rum
2 CONT
2 CONT ABAQA, son of HULAGU Il-Khan & his wife Yesunjin Khatun (Mongolia 1234-Hamadan 1 Apr 1282).  Governor of Khorasan and Mazandaran.  He succeeded his father in 1265 as ABAQA Il-Khan, and was enthroned at Tuzlu Gol 19 Jun 1265 and ag
2 CONC ain at Jaghatu 18 Nov 1270 on receipt of confirmation from the Great Khan.  Vardan's History records that "Abaqa, Hulegu's senior son" was enthroned as Il-Khan after the death of his father by "their relation Teguder, also called 
2 CONC Il-Khan" in [14 Jan 1265/13 Jan 1266][325].  Baptised 1265.  Khan Berke of the Golden Horde invaded Persia in 1266[326].  He defeated the invading forces of the descendants of his great-uncle Chagatai in 1270 at the battle of Hera
2 CONC t[327].  He and his brother led two Ilkhan armies into Syria in Sep 1281 but were defeated by the Mameluks at Homs 30 Oct 1281, after which the Euphrates river was established as the frontier between the two Empires
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ABAQA (Mongolia 1234-Hamadan 1 Apr 1282).  Governor of Khorasan and Mazandaran.  He succeeded his father in 1265 as ABAQA Il-Khan, through the influence of his mother[318], and was enthroned at Tuzlu Gol 19 Jun 1265 and again at J
2 CONC aghatu 18 Nov 1270 on receipt of confirmation from the Great Khan. 
