2 CONC nths, under the leadership of Ilchikdai Noyan, a Mongol commander, fierce battles were fought, resulting in nearly five thousand men from his army being killed or wounded in each conflict... Finally, after the conquest and occupat
2 CONC ion of Herat, and the looting and burning of the city, Ögedai Khan, the son of Genghis Khan – appointed Amir Ezzedin Moghadam to oversee the restoration and repair of the noble city of Herat and other historical and ancient neighb
