1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bajdu
2 CONT Bajdu (died 1295 ) - the ruler of the Ilkhanid dynasty , reigning in 1295.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the grandson of Hulagu , son of Taragaj [1] . He was connected with Iraq and showed great sympathy for Christianity. He took the throne in 1295. However, he did not receive the support of the majority of the emirs [2] . War
2 CONC  broke out between him and Ghazan , the brother of the former Ilkhan. Ghazan's conversion to Islam was a decisive factor in the outcome of the civil war [3] . Thanks to this, he gained many supporters of Bajdu. After the six-month
2 CONC  reign of Bajdu, he was executed on the orders of Ghazan (1295–1304).
