2 CONT Zhí Lǔ Gǔ (直鲁古), also known as Emperor Xian of Western Liao (西辽末帝), was the last ruler of the Western Liao dynasty, which was established by the Khitan people. He reigned from 1177 to 1213 and was the son of Yí Liè (夷列). His rule 
2 CONC marked the end of the Western Liao dynasty, as it was eventually conquered by the Mongol Empire under Genghis Khan.
