1 NAME Pir Husayn (Muhammad Ilkhan) /raised by Jalayerid Hasan Bozorg/
2 GIVN Pir Husayn (Muhammad Ilkhan)
2 _MARNM raised by Jalayerid Hasan Bozorg
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1338
2 PLAC Shahr Naw
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}    PIR HUSAYN ([1326]-executed Shahr-Naw, Alataq [16 Jul] 1338).  He succeeded as MUHAMMAD Il-Khan, in opposition to Musa Il-Khan, proclaimed Il-Khan with the title MUZAFFAR-ed-DIN 20 Jul 1336, enthroned at Qaradar
2 CONC rah 25 Jul 1336.  He was deposed and executed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Muhammad Khan (died July 1338) was a claimant to the throne of the Ilkhanate. He was a great-grandson of Mengu Timur, who was a son of Hulegu. During the breakup of the Ilkhanate following the death of Abu Sa'id in 1335, the Jalay
2 CONC irid Hasan Buzurg raised Muhammad Khan to the throne. Muhammad Khan, who was still a young child, was of Mongol blood and was therefore a way to legitimise Hasan Buzurg's rule from Baghdad. In a battle that took place on July 26, 
2 CONC 1336, Hasan Buzurg and Muhammad Khan defeated the forces of 'Ali Padshah and his puppet Ilkhan, Musa. Hasan Buzurg then installed his claimant in Tabriz. Over the next few years, the two strengthened their hold over western Persia
2 CONC , but the appearance of the Chupanid Hasan Kucek interrupted their plans. The two opposing sides then met in the Alataq area on July 16, 1338, with both Hasan Buzurg and Muhammad Khan suffering defeat. After Hasan Buzurg fled, Muh
2 CONC ammad Khan was captured by the Chupanids and executed.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He was born Pir Husein, a great-grandson of Möngke Temür, a son of Hulagu. His ancestry is cited differently in certain sources - in one source he is shown as a son of Yul Qutlugh b. El-Temür b. Anbarchi b. Mengu Timur and in Mirk
2 CONC hwand he is mentioned as a son of Qutlugh b. Amir Timur b. Anbarchi b. Mengu Timur.
2 CONT Hussein was still a child when he was raised to the throne by Jalayirid Hasan Buzurg and given the regnal name Muhammad Khan. This was done in opposition to his third cousin once removed, Musa. In a battle that took place on July 
2 CONC 26, 1336, Hasan Buzurg and Muhammad Khan defeated the forces of 'Ali Padshah and his puppet, Ilkhan, Musa. Hasan Buzurg then installed his claimant in Tabriz. Jalal ad-Din Zakariyya (or Shams al-Din) and late Mahmudshah Inju's son
2 CONC  Masudshah were appointed as his viziers while Hasan's supporters reaffirmed their positions. Chupanid Sorgan and his mother Sati Beg gained Karabakh, Hajji Taghay reaffirmed in Diyar Bakr, Hajji Tughanak acquired Baghdad, Musa's 
2 CONC would be killer, Emir Qara Hasan granted overlordship over Oirat tribes. However Qara Hasan and Hajji Tughanak couldn't manage to subjugate them and were utterly defeated, latter being killed. Remaining Oirats regrouped under Gove
2 CONC rnor of Khorasan, Shaikh Ali (son of Emir Ali Quschi) and supported Togha Temür for Ilkhanid throne. They were further aided by Ögrünch and Mahmud Esen Qutlugh and even occupied Soltaniyeh for a while. However they were eventually
2 CONC  defeated by Jalayirid army, Ali Padshah's brother Muhammed beg and his wife Qutlugh Malik Khatun (daughter of Gaykhatu) were killed by Kurdish tribesmen, while Oirat leader Shaikh Ali was executed by Arghunshah (son of Emir Nawru
2 CONC z), who wanted Togha Temür to be his own puppet. Ögrünch and Mahmud Esen Qutlugh were too eliminated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Over the next few years, Hasan Buzurg and Muhammad strengthened their hold over western Persia, but the appearance of the Chupanid Hasan Kucek interrupted their plans. Hasan Kucek claimed a Turkish slave of his father's deputy was
2 CONC  in fact, his father Timurtash and arrived from Egypt. This news caused Chupanids to split off from Jalayirids and join Hasan Kucek. The two opposing sides then met in the Ala Tagh area near Van on July 16, 1338, with both Hasan B
2 CONC uzurg and Muhammad Khan suffering defeat. After Hasan Buzurg fled, Muhammad Khan was captured by the Chupanids and executed.
2 CONT ref: https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Muhammad_Khan_(Ilkhan)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Succeeded by Jahan Timur 
2 CONT
2 CONT Muhammad Khan (died July 1338) was a claimant to the throne of the Ilkhanate. He was a great-grandson of Mengu Timur, who was a son of Hulegu.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the breakup of the Ilkhanate following the death of Abu Sa'id in 1335, the Jalayirid Hasan Buzurg raised Muhammad Khan to the throne. Muhammad Khan, who was still a young child, was of Mongol blood and was therefore a way t
2 CONC o legitimise Hasan Buzurg's rule from Baghdad. In a battle that took place on July 26, 1336, Hasan Buzurg and Muhammad Khan defeated the forces of 'Ali Padshah and his puppet Ilkhan, Musa. Hasan Buzurg then installed his claimant 
2 CONC in Tabriz. Over the next few years, the two strengthened their hold over western Persia, but the appearance of the Chupanid Hasan Kucek interrupted their plans. The two opposing sides then met in the Alataq area on July 16, 1338, 
2 CONC with both Hasan Buzurg and Muhammad Khan suffering defeat. After Hasan Buzurg fled, Muhammad Khan was captured by the Chupanids and executed.
