1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_VIII_Palaeologus
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Michael VIII Palaiologos''' or '''Palaeologus''' (Greek: Μιχαὴλ Δούκας Ἄγγελος Κομνηνὸς Παλαιολόγος, romanized: Mikhaēl Doukas Angelos Komnēnos Palaiologos; 1223 – 11 December 1282) reigned as the co-emperor of the Empire of Ni
2 CONC caea from 1259 to 1261, and as Byzantine Emperor from 1261 until his death. Michael VIII was the founder of the Palaiologan dynasty that would rule the Byzantine Empire until the Fall of Constantinople in 1453. He recovered Consta
2 CONC ntinople from the Latin Empire in 1261 and transformed the Empire of Nicaea into a restored Byzantine Empire.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT His reign saw considerable recovery of Byzantine power, including the enlargement of the Byzantine army and navy. It would also include the reconstruction of the city of Constantinople, and the increase of its population.[3] He re
2 CONC established the University of Constantinople, which led to what is regarded as the Palaiologan Renaissance between the 13th and 15th centuries.[3] It was also at this time that the focus of the Byzantine military shifted to the Ba
2 CONC lkans, against the Bulgarians, leaving the Anatolian frontier neglected.[3] His successors could not compensate for this inadequacy, and both the Arsenite schism and two civil wars (cf. Byzantine civil war of 1321–1328, Byzantine 
2 CONC civil war of 1341–1347) undermined further efforts toward territorial consolidation and recovery, draining the empire's strength, economy, and resources. Regular conflict between Byzantine successor states such as the Empire of Th
2 CONC essalonica, Trebizond, Epirus and Serbia resulted in permanent fragmentation of former Byzantine territory and opportunity for increasingly successful conquests of expansive territories by post-Seljuk Anatolian beyliks, most notab
2 CONC ly that of Osman, later called the Ottoman Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_VIII_Palaiologos#Road_to_the_throne Road to the throne]
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_VIII_Palaiologos#Constantinople Constantinople]
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_VIII_Palaiologos#Diplomacy_and_conquest Diplomacy and conquest]
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_VIII_Palaiologos#Michael_and_Charles_of_Anjou Michael and Charles of Anjou]
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_VIII_Palaiologos#Council_of_Lyons_and_after Council of Lyons and after]
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_VIII_Palaiologos#Sicilian_Vespers Sicilian Vespers]
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_VIII_Palaiologos#Legacy Legacy]
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_VIII_Palaiologos#Family Family]
2 CONT
