2 CONT Yí Liè (夷列), a historical figure connected to the Yélǜ (耶律) family, which played a significant role in the Khitan-led Liao dynasty of China. Yí Liè, also known as 遼仁宗 (Liáo Rén Zōng), was related to prominent members of the family
2 CONC  such as 耶律大石 (Yélǜ Dàshí). He lived during the 12th century and passed away in 1163.
