1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Chinggis Khan (Genghis, 1206–27) gave his sister Temülün to Botu of the Ikires clan. Botu's son Sorqaq received as a bride Altu, the daughter of Köchü, the son of Chinggis's son Ögedei. Meanwhile, Ula'adai, Botu's 
2 CONC son, gave his daughter Qutuqtai to Möngke, the son of Chinggis's son Tolui. Sorqaq's son '''Jaqurchin''' married '''Yisünjin''', the daughter of '''Alchidai''', the son of Chinggis's brother '''Qachi'un'''. Several generations lat
2 CONC er this intermarriage continued. The chief wife of Emperor Shidebala (titled Yingzong, 1320–23) was an Ikires princess, Sügebala, whose father was '''Ashi''', son of Jaqurchin's son Qurin; her mother was Ili-Qaya, the daughter of 
2 CONC Emperor Temür, son of Jingim, son of Tolui's son Qubilai. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From: Encyclopedia of Mongolia and the Mongol Empire. 
