2 CONT
2 CONT On 25 July 1261, Alexios Strategopoulos captured Constantinople, capital of the Latin Empire. Most troops of the rival Empire were in campaign and would never return to their capital. Latin Emperor Baldwin II of Courtenay escaped 
2 CONC in a Venetian galley to Negropont and would remain in exile for the rest of his life.
