2 CONT 4.         '''IOANNES Doukas Palaiologos''' ([1225/30]-[1273/74]).  Georgios Phrantzes names "Michael Comnenus, Constantinus Palaeologus et Iohannes" as the three sons of "Androniko Palaeologo…magnum domesticum"[58].  Georgios Akr
2 CONC opolites records that Emperor Mikhael VIII invested "fratrem germanium suum Ioannem Comnenum" as "magnum domesticum…[et] sebastocratorem"[59].  Ephræmius records that Mikhael Palaiologos invested "Comnenum Ioannem fratrem suum" as
2 CONC  "sebastocratorem"[60].  Megas domestikos 1258.  Sébastokrator 1259.  Despot 1261/63.  Under his leadership, Byzantine troops defeated the Sicilian/Achaian/Epirote alliance in the valley of Pelagonia in Autumn 1259, and again defe
2 CONC ated Mikhael II Angelos Despot of Epirus in 1264.  A short chronicle records the death in 1273/74 of Ioannes Palaiologos[61].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ([1259]) --- Tornikaine, daughter of KONSTANTINOS Tornikios & his wife ---.  Pachymeres records the marriage of "Constantini Tornicii filiam" and "fratrem…Ioannes" (referring to the future Emperor Mikhael VIII)[62].  Her p
2 CONC arentage is confirmed by Ephræmius which records that "sebastocrator…Ioannes cum Constantino socero Tornice" met the emperor at "Lampsaci"[63]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT    Ioannes Palaiologos & his wife had [two] children:
