1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [4.         JANI BEG (-murdered 1357).  Howorth names “Sheritumgha, the mother of Janibeg, and probably also of his other sons Timur, Tinibeg and Khidrbeg” as one of the wives of Uzbek[166].  He seized control from
2 CONC  his brother and succeeded in 1342 as JANI BEG Khan of the Golden Horde.  He was murdered by his son Berdibek[167].  Howorth records that Jani Beg returned to Kipchak and, falling ill, summoned his son Berdi Beg to install him as 
2 CONC his successor but that “fearing that his father might recover, Berdibeg murdered him”[168].  Six children: ...] 9b)        [...  twelve sons (-killed 1357).  Howorth records that Jani Beg returned to Kipchak and, falling ill, summ
2 CONC oned his son Berdi Beg to install him as his successor but that “fearing that his father might recover, Berdibeg murdered him”, adding that “according to Russian authors, he proceeded to put to death twelve of his brothers” on his
2 CONC  accession[171]. ref: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MONGOLS.htm#Toghrilcha
2 CONT ===
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jani_Beg Wikipedia]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.revolvy.com/topic/Jani%20Beg&item_type=topic
2 CONT GOLDEN HORD Dirigeant de Kipchak دشت قبچاق
2 CONT
2 CONT After his brother Tiny Beg who died in 1340, Jani Beg I  was the last member of the House of Juchi to rule over the Kipchak Qanate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jani Beg (died 1357) was a khan of the Golden Horde from 1342 to 1357, succeeding his father Öz Beg Khan.
2 CONT
2 CONT After putting two of his brothers to death, Jani Beg crowned himself in Saray-Jük. He is known to have actively interfered in the affairs of Russian principalities and of Lithuania. The Grand Princes of Moscow, Simeon Gordiy, and 
2 CONC Ivan II, were under constant political and military pressure from Jani Beg.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1356 Jani Beg conducted a military campaign in Azerbaijan and conquered the city of Tabriz, installing his own governor there. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Defeats and executes Malik Ashraf the ruler of Azarbaijan (the son of Timurtash)
2 CONT
2 CONT [ Joni Beig entered Azarbaijan in 1379 AD and murdered Malek Ashraf in Tabriz. In this way the Chupani dynasty was terminated] [Jani Beig Uzbek, upon killing Malik Ashraf, had appointed his son Bardi Beig as governor of Azarbaijan
2 CONC . But he sometime later left Tabriz and gave the position to Akhi Juq. Sultan Oveys attacked Tabriz and in 1380 AD entered it. In this way, Azarbaijan, too, fell to the Jalayerids. (ref page 194 Iranian History at a glance http://
2 CONC bit.ly/1Pu8qqA
2 CONT
2 CONT He also asserted Jochid dominance over the Chagatai Khanate, attempting to unite the three khanates of the Mongol Empire. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [ Janibek (some sources Chanibek [1] , d. 1357 ) ( tat. Җanibәk, Canibäk) - Golden Horde Khan, the third son of Uzbek Khan , Khan of the Golden Horde ( 1342 - 1357 ). As a result of a successful war with Persia joined by Azerbaija
2 CONC n, bringing the Golden Horde reached its maximum size, including West Siberia, Bulgarian Ulus (Middle Volga region), some of the territory of Russia were in the political dependence, the White Horde (Kazakhstan, Khorezm), the Blue
2 CONC  Horde (Kuban Don, Crimea), the Caucasus Ulus (including Azerbaijan).
2 CONT
2 CONT He came to power as a result of the murder of his supporters brothers - Khan Tini Beg and Hızır. He carried out a policy of strengthening the central government and interference in the affairs of the vassal principalities. However
2 CONC , Janibek in Russian chronicles called "good" [1] . In 1347 there was only one for all the reign Djanibek foray into Russia - in the vicinity of the city Alexina ]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT  Zarb Saray al-Jadid, 753 in a number of lines, all within a hexafoil / Flower ornament, no inscriptions. Dated to 753 AH/1352 AD). 17mm, 1.67 grams. Mint of Saray al-Jadid. Fedorov-Davidov #104ff; Yanina V #31ff.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jani Beg (died 1357) was a khan of the Golden Horde from 1342 to 1357, succeeding his father Uzbeg Khan. After putting two of his brothers to death, Jani Beg crowned himself in Saray-Jük. He is known to have actively interfered in
2 CONC  the affairs of Russian principalities and of Lithuania. The Grand Princes of Moscow, Simeon Gordiy, and Ivan II, were under constant political and military pressure from Jani Beg. Jani Beg commanded a massive Crimean Tatar force 
2 CONC that attacked the Crimean port city of Kaffa in 1343. The siege was lifted by an Italian relief force in February. In 1345 Jani Beg again besieged Kaffa, however, his assault was again unsuccessful due to an outbreak of the Black 
2 CONC Plague among his troops. It is thought that Jani Beg's army catapulted infected corpses into Kaffa in an attempt to use the Black Death to weaken the defenders. Infected Genoese sailors subsequently sailed from Kaffa to Genoa, int
2 CONC roducing the Black Death into Europe. The reign of Jani Beg was marked by the first signs of the feudal strife which would eventually contribute to the demise of the Golden Horde. Jani Beg's assassination in 1357 opened a quarter-
2 CONC century of political turmoil within the Golden Horde. ref. http://www.numismall.com/acc/Anonymous-copper-pulo-of-Khan-Jani-Beg-1342-1357-AD-Saray-al-Jadid-mint-1352-AD-Mongols-of-the-Golden-Horde-Fedorov-Davidov-104.html
