1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Russia's Chudov Monastery, founded at about the time of Jani Beg's fall by Metropolitan Aleksii and Sergei of Radonezh was built on land that, according to legend, the Khan had granted to Aleksii as thanks for the 
2 CONC miraculous curing of his mother, Taidula, by the latter. (profile photo is Metropolitan Alexis Healing the Tatar Queen Taidula from Blindness while Janibeg Looks on, Yakov Kapkov (1816-54).
2 CONT
2 CONT JANI BEG (-murdered 1357).  Howorth names “Sheritumgha, the mother of Janibeg, and probably also of his other sons Timur, Tinibeg and Khidrbeg” as one of the wives of Uzbek. (ref: Howorth 1880: 172 considers her the mother of Jani
2 CONC  Beg and "and probably also of his other sons," contradicting contemporary sources. Howorth, Henry Hoyle (2008-01-01). History of the Mongols from the 9th to the 19th Century: The So-Called Tartars of Russia and Central Asia. Cosi
2 CONC mo, Inc. p. 172. ISBN 978-1-60520-134-4. - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%96zbeg_Khan)  
2 CONT
2 CONT He seized control from his brother and succeeded in 1342 as JANI BEG Khan of the Golden Horde.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was murdered by his son Berdibek.  Howorth records that Jani Beg returned to Kipchak and, falling ill, summoned his son Berdi Beg to install him as his successor but that “fearing that his father might recover, Berdibeg murdere
2 CONC d him”
2 CONT ===
2 CONT I am told that her father was not Daniel Alexandrovitch of Moscou,  quote: Merci d'indiquer sur quoi vous vous fondez pour maintenir ce profil. Je soutiens que cette personne n'a jamais existé ; la liste des enfants du Prince Dani
2 CONC el de Moscou (que j'ai dans mes ancêtres) est connue, il a marié son fils à une sœur de Ouzbek-khan, ça oui ; mais nulle source sérieuse (universitaire, scientifique) à ma connaissance n'attribue à Daniel de fille, femme du khan. 
2 CONC Je considère qu'il faut l'effacer, c'est clairement une erreur.] unquote
2 CONT but I have read that she was indeed Prince Daniel's wife in many places. 
2 CONT One of them:
2 CONT Daniyl Aleksandrovich of Moscow (born Rurikid of Vladimir), Grand Prince of Moscow, 1261 - 1303
2 CONT Daniyl, Aleksandrovich, Даниил, Александрович, Danila, Aleksandrovičus of Moscow, Московский was born on month day 1261, in birth place , to Alexander Nevsky, Yaroslavich, Александр "Невский", Ярославич, Aleksandras Neviškis and A
2 CONC leksandra, Praskowija, Aleksandra, Praskovija, Александра, Параскева Polockietė .
2 CONT Daniyl was baptized in baptism place .
2 CONT Daniyl had 4 siblings: Eudoxia Aleksandrovna Евдокия Александровна Jevdokija Aleksandraitė and 3 other siblings .
2 CONT Daniyl married Maria, Glebovna, Мария, Глебовна, Marija .
2 CONT They had 8 children: Sheritumgha , Yuriy Danilovich Юрий Даниилович Jurijus Danilovičius and 6 other children .
