1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Umar_Shaikh_Mirza_I
2 CONT *https://www.wikiwand.com/en/Umar_Shaikh_Mirza_I 
2 CONT Umar Shaikh Mirza was one of four sons of Timur who survived infancy. His mother Tolun Agha was a concubine.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ... In 1376, Timur appointed him governor of Ferghana.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1393, Timur defeated the Persian Muzaffarid dynasty with the capture and execution of its final monarch Shah Mansur. Timur bestowed the kingdom's former territory of Fars on Umar Shaikh to administer as governor.[8] The prince'
2 CONC s former post of Ferghana was given to his son Iskandar Mirza.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT However, Umar Shaikh was not able to hold this post for long. In 1394, whilst answering summons from his father, Umar Shaikh was killed after being shot in the neck by an arrow fired from the Kurdish fortress of Kharmatu, near the
2 CONC  city of Baghdad.[8][4] Timur reportedly did not show any emotion upon learning of his son's death.[10]
2 CONT
2 CONT Umar Shaikh's governorship was given to his eldest son Pir Muhammad, while his body was escorted by his wives and his younger son Iskandar to the city of Kesh (modern day Shahrisabz).[11] Here, he was buried alongside his brother 
2 CONC in the Tomb of Jahangir, part of the Dorussaodat mausoleum complex. Presently, the tomb is the best surviving part of the structure.[12]
