1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hasan-Jalal also attempted to strengthen his alliances with the Mongols by having his daughter Rhuzukan marry Bora Noyan, the son of a Mongol leader.]?  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Hasan-Jalalyan
2 CONT
2 CONT ====
2 CONT
2 CONT [ The Celali rebellions broke out in response to economic crisis facing the Ottoman Empire and the spread of firearms to the countryside in the late sixteenth century. The Celalis were composed of disgruntled cavalrymen whose
2 CONT timars were shrinking in size landless peasants and part-time soldiers equipped with firearms and unemployed seminary students. The Celalis roamed the countryside, plundered villages, causing peasants to flee take shelter in the c
2 CONC ities. The Ottoman army was unable to completely defeat the Celalis and the state tried co-opt many leaders with the promise of title and land. But the Celali rebellion of the late sixteenth century continued into the seventeenth 
2 CONC century and coincided with the Ottoman-Iranian wars of 1603-1607.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many Celali leaders defected as a group to Iran since Shah 'Abbas I (1587- 1629) provided them with open support. ] ref: The Celali reballion. https://www.academia.edu/3884811/Rebels_and_Renegades_on_Ottoman-Iranian_Borderlands_Po
2 CONC rous_Frontiers_and_Hybrid_Identities
