1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shem-Tov_ibn_Falaquera '''Shem-Tov ben Joseph ibn Falaquera''' (Palquera)] (Hebrew: שם טוב בן יוסף אבן פלקירה‎; 1225 – c. 1290) was a Spanish Jewish philosopher and poet and commentat
2 CONC or. A vast body of work is attributed to Falaquera, including encyclopedias of Arabic and Greek philosophies, maqamas, some 20,000 poetic verses, and commentaries on Maimonides’ Guide to the Perplexed. The common theme in Falaquer
2 CONC a’s writing was to encourage observant Jews to study philosophy and to appreciate the harmony that existed between Torah and rational truth learned in philosophy. While Falaquera did not advocate teaching the secrets of science an
2 CONC d divine sciences to every man, he did advocate the teaching of these truths to a broader range of educated Jewish males than previous proponents of rationalist thinking.
