1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Please, don't connect wife of Daniel of Moscow with certain family! Her ancestry is unknown and not cited in contemporary sources.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In more current sources her name is cited as:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1) Agrippina'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2) Eudokia (Eudoxia) Aleksandrovna (may be from Murom dukes)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3) dau of Lev of Halicz"
2 CONT
2 CONT '''But it's not enough to connect her with certain parents!'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of Daniel's wife is mentioned in the Rostov Cathedral Synodikon published in 1996, where she is named Agrippina. According to A. A. Gorsky's assumption, she was the daughter of Lev Danilovich. P.V. Dolgorukov calls her Ev
2 CONC dokia Alexandrovna.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Долгоруков П. В. Российская родословная книга. — СПб.: Типография Карла Вингебера, 1854. — Т. 1. — С. 232.
