1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Qaidu Khan's father was **Orus**. He was a prominent figure in the early Mongol Empire and a member of the **Borjigin** clan, which was the same clan as Genghis Khan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Here's a brief overview:
2 CONT
2 CONT ### Orus
2 CONT - **Role**: Orus was a Mongol chieftain and the father of Qaidu Khan. His leadership and lineage contributed to the prominence of the Borjigin clan.
2 CONT - **Historical Context**: Orus was part of the broader network of Mongol leaders that shaped the early history of the Mongol Empire. His son, Qaidu Khan, played a significant role in the politics of the Chagatai Khanate and the Mo
2 CONC ngol Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Orus is a notable figure in Mongol history due to his connection to Qaidu Khan, who was a key leader during the late 13th and early 14th centuries.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT founding father of the most prominent labor (noyankin, Tayichi'ut, aralud, Kujat-Gerges, haburhod, sunid, honghotan, oronar). The brothers stripped him and kicked
2 CONT
2 CONT in  " Histoire Secrète des Mongols "   "Secrète " au sens de " Réservée" aux descendants de Gengis~Qahan   ~~Restitution du texte mongol et traduction française des chapitres I à VI.  ~~Paul Pelliot  (oeuvres posthumes),  Paris,  
2 CONC 1949.
2 CONT
