1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Mstislav Yurievich''' (d. after 1161) - Prince of Peresopnitsa (1150), Novgorod (1156-1157), son of Yuri Dolgorukiy.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the first capture of Kyiv, Yuri Dolgorukiy was appointed as governor in Peresopnitsa - in the principality center in Volyn, which belonged to Yuri's opponent Izyaslav Mstislavich. After the final approval of Yuri in Kyiv (11
2 CONC 55), Mstislav became his father's representative in Novgorod the Great. After the death of his father (1157), Mstislav, along with most of his brothers, went north, and in 1161 he was sent by Andrey, together with his mother and b
2 CONC rothers Vasilko and Vsevolod, to Byzantium, where he was received with great honor by Emperor Manuel and received from him the Oskalana region.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to the daughter of the Novgorod boyar Pyotr Mikhalkovich. Historian F. B. Uspensky points out that some researchers consider Rognvald Ulvsson, a relative of Ingigerda of Kyiv, to be the ancestor of the Novgorodians 
2 CONC Mikhalkovichi - this connection could cause marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT He left his only son, Yaroslav the Red.
