2 CONT
2 CONT Attributes Robed as a Russian Great Prince, often wearing armor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Patronage Soldiers, Borders of Russia
2 CONT
2 CONT Saint Alexander Nevsky listen (help·info) (Алекса́ндр Яросла́вич Не́вский in Russian; transliteration: Aleksandr Yaroslavich Nevskij) (May 30, 1220? – November 14, 1263) was the Grand Prince of Novgorod and Vladimir during some of
2 CONC  the most trying times in the country's history. Commonly regarded as the key figure of medieval Russia, Alexander was the grandson of Vsevolod the Big Nest and rose to legendary status on account of his military victories over th
2 CONC e German invaders while employing shrewd conciliatory policies towards the powerful Golden Horde.
2 CONT
