1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ivan I of Moscow From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Marriages and children Ivan was married twice. His first wife was named Helena. They had at least eight children: Simeon of Moscow (7 November 1316 - 27 April 
2 CONC 1353). Daniil Ivanovich (c. 1320 - 1328). Fefinia Ivanovna. Maria Ivanovna (d. 2 June 1365). Married Konstantin Vasilievich, Prince of Rostov (d. 1365). Their daughter Vasilisa of Rostov married Dmitry of Suzdal. Through her they 
2 CONC were grandparents of Eudoxia of Moscow. Ivan II of Moscow (30 March 1326 - 13 November 1353). Andrei Ivanovich, Prince of Novgorod (4 August 1327 - 6 June 1353). Death attributed to the Black Death. Eudoxia Ivanovna. (d. 1342). Ma
2 CONC rried Vasily Mikhailovich, Prince of Yaroslavl (d. 1345). Fedosia Ivanovna (d. 1365).
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
