2 CONT She also had a sister, who became the wife of Emir Musa from the Taichuyut tribe....] ... [Many believe that Sarai-mulk khanum was Tamerlane's most beloved wife, but in reality this marriage was only political. Although she never 
2 CONC had a chance to give birth to children from her second husband, she enjoyed his unconditional trust and had great authority at court. An example of this is the story of Shad Mulk . When it was discovered that Khalil Sultan had mar
2 CONC ried her, a woman of low birth, Timurordered her to be executed. But Sarai-mulk khanum intervened in the matter and stood up for the “unexpected” daughter-in-law, her main argument was that Shad-mulk was pregnant. As a result, Tim
2 CONC ur saved her life. Sarai-mulk khanim raised most of Timur's children and grandchildren, among them were Shahrukh and Khalil Sultan ....]
