2 CONT Tokhtamysh kills his wife "Tovlunbek."
2 CONT Among others, Tokhtamysh had married the widow of Mamai, probably identical with a daughter of Berdi Beg and with the Tulun Beg Khanum who had briefly ruled at Sarai in 1370–1371; in 1386 he had her executed, apparently for partic
2 CONC ipating in an obscure conspiracy.[38] According to the Muʿizz al-ansāb, Tokhtamysh had eight sons and five daughters, as well as six grandchildren, as follows.[39]
