2 CONT '''Amadeus VI''' (4 January 1334 – 1 March 1383), nicknamed '''the Green Count''' (Italian: ''Il Conte Verde'') was Count of Savoy from 1343 to 1383. He was the eldest son of Aymon, Count of Savoy, and Yolande Palaeologina of Mont
2 CONC ferrat. Though he started under a regency, he showed himself to be a forceful leader, continuing Savoy's emergence as a power in Europe politically and militarily. He participated in a crusade against the Turks who were moving int
2 CONC o Europe.  
2 CONT
