2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         MANUEL Palaiologos Kantakouzenos ([1326]-Mistra 10 Apr 1380).  Nicephoras Gregoras names "duo imperatoris filii Matthæus et Manuel" (referring to Emperor Ioannes VI Kantakouzenos)[553].  Kephale of Berrhoia 1343/47.  Hi
2 CONC s father installed him as Despot in Morea in May 1347.  His capital Mistra became a thriving cultural centre[554].  Eparchos of Constantinople 1348/49.  Emperor Ioannes V confirmed his appointment in [1356] after unsuccessfully at
2 CONC tempting to displace him in favour of his cousins Mikhael Asen and Andreas Asen[555].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Betrothed''' (Jul 1342, contract broken [1346/47] ) to ANNA [Maria] Oliver, daughter of JOVAN Oliver Voivode of Ovčepolje and Lesovo, Serbian despot[556] & his [---] wife ---.  Ioannes Kantakouzenos records the betrothal of "Ma
2 CONC nuele iuniori filio" and "Liberi filiam", in a passage dated to [1342][557].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (betrothed [1341], after May 1347) ZAMPEA [Isabelle] de Lusignan, daughter of CONSTANTINE II King of Armenia & his second wife --- (-in Cyprus [1382/87] ).  Ioannes Kantakouzenos records the betrothal of "imperatore, Manue
2 CONC li filio" and "Syrgem Ntelensuziam, imperatoris Andronici consobrinum, Cypriorum regis filium…filiam", in a passage dated to [1341], the same source recording in a later passage that "Syrgen" terminated the betrothal after learnin
2 CONC g of Manuel's betrothal in 1342 to "Liberi filiam"[558].  The Chronicle of Jean Dardel names "madame Ysabel de Lisegnan, fille du…roy Guy d'Armenye", when recording that Pierre I King of Cyprus met her at "Moudon"[559].  She was k
2 CONC nown as MARIA or MARGARETA in Greece.  The Chronicle of Amadi records that "madama Margarita de Lusignan, nezza del signor de Sur et sorella del re Livon de Armenia, relitta del quondam Manoel Catacusino despotto della Morea" came
2 CONC  to Cyprus in 1372[560]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
