2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00049917&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Andronikos Komnenos (or Andronicus Comnenus) (Greek: Ανδρόνικος Κομνηνός) (c. 1108–1142)''' was the third child and second son of the Byzantine Emperor John II Komnenos and his Hungarian wife, Piroska (Eirene).
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Andronikos Komnenos''' was married to a woman named Eirene (Aineiadissa ?), by whom he had several children, these were:
2 CONT #Maria Komnene, who married Theodoros Dasiotes, then John Kantakouzenos.[2]
2 CONT #John Doukas Komnenos (d. c. 17 September 1176), who married (first name unknown) Taronitissa, and had a daughter Maria.[3]
2 CONT #Theodora Komnene (d. 2 January 1184), who married Henry II Jasomirgott,[4] and had three children, including Leopold V of Austria.[citation needed]
2 CONT #Eudokia Komnene, who married an unknown first husband and then Michael Gabras. She was also one of the mistresses of Andronikos I Komnenos.[5]
2 CONT #Alexios Komnenos, (murd. 1183), who was married to Maria Doukaina, and had two short-lived sons. He is believed to have had Maria of Antioch (widow of Manuel I) as a mistress. He headed the regency council for her son, Alexios II
2 CONC .[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sebastokrator Andronikos Komnenos was born circa 1108. He was the son of Ioannes II Kaloiannis Komnenos, basileus Rhomaiôn and Piroska, Hercegnõ Magyarország. Sebastokrator Andronikos Komnenos married sebastokratorissa Eirene Rhod
2 CONC ocanakis, daughter of Andronikos Rhodocanakis and Theodora Tarchaniotes.3,4 Sebastokrator Andronikos Komnenos died in 1141. Died in the Fall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family sebastokratorissa Eirene Rhodocanakis b. 1109, d. 1162 Children	 Theodora Komnene+ b. c 1128, d. 1184 protosebastos Ioannes Komnenos b. c 1129, d. 1174 protostrator Alexios Komnenos+ b. c 1132, d. 1183
2 CONT
2 CONT http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p366.htm#i9228
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Nació en Balalista, Grecia, en 1108, y murió en 1142. Hijo de Juan II Comnene, nacido el 24-III-1087/1088. Murto el 5-VII-1143 en Taurus, Turquía. Casó en 1104 con Prisca (Irene) de Hungría (1075 a 10-XII-1134, en Bitinia, Turquía
2 CONC ), hija de San Ladislao de Hungría y Adelaida von Rheinfelden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Casó, en 1124, con Irene Aineidasa (nacida después de 1100 y fallecida en Protocrator, Grecia, en 1152. Tuvieron por hijos a Eudoxia Comnene (desp. de 1128; casó con Andrónico I Comnene -1110 a 1185-, y tuvieron por hija a Irene C
2 CONC omnene, esposa de Isaac II Angelos, emperador de Bizancio: ver Dinastía Angelos) y a Alexis Comnene que nació en 1130 y murió en 1183. Casó el 2-IV-1162 con María Dukaina. Tuvieron por hija Eudoxia Comnene (c.1162 a 3-II-1202/1203
2 CONC ), que casó con Guillermo VIII, señor de Montpellier.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The family of Andronic COMNÈNE and Irène .. [132087] COMNÈNE, Andronic (Jean II & PRISKA dit Irène de HONGRIE [132088]), sébastrocrate
2 CONT * married about 1130 .., Irène (..) 1) Jean, protosébaste, duc de Chypre, married about 1155 Marie TARONITÈS
2 CONT
