1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTIUM%2010571204.htm#EvdokiaKM1ThorosIIMountains
2 CONT
2 CONT d)         '''EVDOKIA Komnene'''.  Niketas Choniates names "Alexius, Andronicus et…Isaacius" as the three brothers of Emperor Manuel, stating that Andronikos left daughters "Mariam, Theodoram et Eudociam", adding that Evdokia beca
2 CONC me the mistress of Andronikos Komnenos after the death of her husband[324].  This must refer to a first marriage which is unrecorded elsewhere, as her marriage to Mikhael Gabras is recorded subsequent to her affair with Andronikos
2 CONC  Komnenos.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Europäische Stammtafeln[325] suggests that Evdokia married firstly ([1140/42], '''divorced''' 1149) Thoros II Lord of the Mountains, but there seems to be no basis for this.  Rüdt-Collenberg says that "a first marriage with a Byza
2 CONC ntine princess, mentioned by Tchamitch for the years 1140-1142, is more than doubtful"[326].  In any case, assuming that the report by Niketas Choniates is correct, Evdokia's first marriage was ended by the death of her husband, n
2 CONC ot divorce.  In a later passage, Niketas Choniates records the marriage of "Eudocia Comnenia Andronici amica" and "Michæle…Gabra"[327].  Ioannes Kinnamos records that "Michael cognomento Gabras" married "ex fratre Manuelis neptim"
2 CONC [328].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly --- (-1150 or before).  The identity of Evdokia's first husband is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mistress''' ([1150/52]) of her cousin ANDRONIKOS Komnenos, who later succeeded as Emperor ANDRONIKOS I.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ([1152/53]) MIKHAEL Gabras, son of --- (-after 1170).  Sébastos. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
