2 CONT
2 CONT Theodoros I Laskaris was emperor of Nicaea (1204–1221), was born of a noble Byzantine family. He became the son-in-law of the Emperor Alexius III.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: event 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1204.
2 CONT
2 CONT ·expelled from Constantinople by the Latins, and gathering a band of refugees, first at Brusa and then at Nicaea (modern Iznik), across the Bosporus in Asia Minor, and formed a new Byzantine state 
2 CONT
2 CONT event 
2 CONT
2 CONT BETWEEN 1203 AND 1204, in Byzantine Empire. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ·distinguished himself during the sieges of Constantinople by the Latins in the Fourth Crusade 
2 CONT
2 CONT event 
2 CONT
2 CONT AFT 1204.
2 CONT
2 CONT ·recognized as the Byzantine government-in-exile and as the legitimate successor of the Byzantine Empire during the crusaders' occupation of Constantinople 
2 CONT
2 CONT event 
2 CONT
2 CONT ·a son-in-law of the Byzantine emperor Alexius III Angelus 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1208.
2 CONT
2 CONT ·assumed the title of emperor and defended his infant empire not only against the crusaders but also against David Comnenus, a rival Greek emperor in Trebizond to the east on the Black Sea, and against the Seljuq Turks, 
2 CONT
2 CONT event 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1211, in spring. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ·not persuaded to abdicate by the Seljuq sultan of Rum, Kay-Khusraw, who had given asylum to the emperor Alexius, and when Kay-Khusraw invaded his territory in the spring, he defeated and killed Kay in battle, and also captured an
2 CONC d imprisoned Alexius, 
2 CONT
2 CONT ABT 1214.
2 CONT
2 CONT ·signed a treaty, following a period of war with Henry of Flanders, defining the frontiers between the Greek empire of Nicaea and the Latin empire of Constantinople 
2 CONT
2 CONT event 
2 CONT
2 CONT ABT 1215.
2 CONT
2 CONT ·annexed much of the territory of Trebizond
2 CONT
2 CONT event 
2 CONT
2 CONT AFT 1216.
2 CONT
2 CONT ·strengthened his ties to the Latin empire, following Henry's death, by taking as his third wife Maria, daughter of the empress Yolande 
2 CONT
2 CONT event 
2 CONT
2 CONT Aug 1219.
2 CONT
2 CONT ·made a lucrative commercial agreement with the Venetians in Constantinople  
2 CONT
2 CONT BEF Nov 1221.
2 CONT
2 CONT ·negotiated a settlement with Yolande's son and successor as Latin emperor, Robert of Courtenay, to whom he betrothed his daughter Eudocia 
