1 NOTE Kalman I of the 2nd Kingdom of Bulgaria was poisoned by his stepmother, and died 1246.  He was succeeded by his half brother, Michael.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kalman I of Bulgaria was poisoned by his stepmother in 1246.  She had arranged this so her son Michael Asen, his half brother, could succeed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kalman I of Bulgaria, son of Ivan Asen II, succeeded his father to the throne in 1241.  He ruled until 1246.
