1 NOTE {geni:about_me} When Timur died in 1405, Nasir-ad-Din Faraj, the Mamluk Sultan of Egypt, released Sultan Ahmed, who returned to Baghdad, and Qara Yusuf, who took up residence in Tabriz. In spite of their agreement, however, it did
2 CONC  not last. Ahmed wanted to regain Azerbaijan as a result he attacked the Kara Koyunlu. He managed to occupy Tabriz for a brief time, but was defeated in August 1410. He was then captured by Qara Yusuf and executed; Ahmed's son Ala
2 CONC -ud-Daula, who had been released by the Timurids, was also killed. Ahmed's nephew Shah Walad Jalayir briefly succeeded him in Baghdad but the Kara Koyunlu took the city a year later.
