1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Sultan Abu Al-Nasr Sayf ad-Din Al-Ashraf Qaitbay''' (Arabic: السلطان أبو النصر سيف الدين الأشرف قايتباي; c. 1416/1418 – 7 August 1496)[a] was the eighteenth Burji Mamluk Sultan of Egypt from 872 to 901 A.H. (146
2 CONC 8–1496 C.E.). He was Circassian by birth, and was purchased by the ninth sultan Barsbay (1422 to 1438 C.E.) before being freed by the eleventh Sultan Jaqmaq (1438 to 1453 C.E.). During his reign, he stabilized the Mamluk state and
2 CONC  economy, consolidated the northern boundaries of the Sultanate with the Ottoman Empire, engaged in trade with other contemporaneous polities, and emerged as a great patron of art and architecture. In fact, although Qaitbay fought
2 CONC  sixteen military campaigns, he is best remembered for the spectacular building projects that he sponsored, leaving his mark as an architectural patron on Mecca, Medina, Jerusalem, Damascus, Aleppo, Alexandria, and every quarter o
2 CONC f Cairo. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qaitbay En], [https://tr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kay%C4%B1tbay Tr]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qaitbay#Family Family]
2 CONT
2 CONT One of his wives was the [https://www.geni.com/people/daughter-of-Sultan-Sayf-ad-Din-Inal/6000000204994423942 daughter] of Sultan Sayf ad-Din Inal. [15] Another wife was [https://www.geni.com/people/Khawand-Aslbay/6000000204962569
2 CONC 827 Khawand Aslbay], a Circassian,[16] and sister of Sultan [https://www.geni.com/people/Abu-Sa-id-Qansuh-23rd-Mamluk-Sultan-of-Egypt-and-Syria/6000000204991425876 Abu Sa'id Qansuh]. She was the mother of his son, Sultan [https://
2 CONC www.geni.com/people/An-Nasir-Muhammad-ibn-Qaitbay/6000000204962211875 Sultan An-Nasir Muhammad]. After Qaitbay's death, she married Sultan [https://www.geni.com/people/Al-Ashraf-Abu-al-Nasir-Janbalat-Mamluk-Sultan-of-Egypt-and-Syr
2 CONC ia/6000000204992101840 Al-Ashraf Janbalat].[15] Another wife was [https://www.geni.com/people/Khawand-Fatima/6000000204952942836 Khawand Fatima], the daughter of Ala al-Din Ali bin Ali bin Al-Khassbak.[16] She was the mother of [h
2 CONC ttps://www.geni.com/people/Ahmed-bin-Qaitbay/6000000204962956825 Ahmed] (1462 – 1468) and [https://www.geni.com/people/Sitti-al-Jarakisa-bin-Qaitbay/6000000204962511886 Sitt al-Jarakisa] (1464 – 1468).[17][18] After Qaitbay's deat
2 CONC h, she married Sultans [https://www.geni.com/people/Tuman-bay-I-25th-Mamluk-Sultan-of-Egypt-and-Syria/6000000204961474882 Tuman bay I] [15] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Al-Ashraf-Qansuh-al-Ghuri-Mamluk-Sultan-of-Egypt/60000002
2 CONC 04944802821 Al-Ashraf Qansuh al-Ghuri].[19] She died on 6 June 1504.[16] Another wife was [https://www.geni.com/people/Khawand-Zaynab/6000000204962571827 Khawand Zaynab].[20] 
2 CONT
