1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Mikhail Vsevolodovich''' (Kir-Mikhail; died July 20, 1217, Isady) - prince of Pronsk (1207-1217 intermittently), son of Vsevolod Glebovich, who reigned after the death of his father. Principle Prince of Pronsk, 
2 CONC from Rurik XI generation.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1207, after the invasion of the Grand Duchy of Ryazan, Vsevolod "the Big Nest" left Pronsk for Chernigov, the defense of Pronsk was led by his cousin Izyaslav Vladimirovich, but was defeated, and Oleg Vladimirovich was imprison
2 CONC ed in the Principality of Pronsk. In the winter of 1208/1209, Mikhail Vsevolodovich and Izyaslav Vladimirovich invaded the Vladimir-Suzdal principality but were defeated in the vicinity of Moscow by Prince Yuri Vsevolodovich of Vl
2 CONC adimir. On July 20, 1217, Mikhail was killed by Gleb and Konstantin Vladimirovich at the princely congress in Isady.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mikhail is mentioned in the “Tale of the Devastation of Ryazan by Batu” (erroneously) as a prince who, after the invasion, received the reign of Pronsk from Ingvar Ingvarevich of Ryazan (mentioned only in this work).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family and Children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Mikhail was married to Vera-Alyona (Olyona) - the daughter of the Grand Duke of Chernigov Vsevolod Chermny; the Ipatiev Chronicle mentions his son (Kyur Mikhailovich), who brought news of the Mongol invasion to Vladimir in 1237 (a
2 CONC nd died during the invasion). According to the BDT version, the son of Mikhail was called Vsevolod.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm#MikhailVsevolodichdied1317 Medlands]
