1 OCCU Prins av Belz, Kung av Galicia-Volhynia och Rus, Kung i Galicien 1301-08, князь Белзкий (1269—1301), король Галицкой Руси (с 1301)
1 TITL King
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://finnholbek.dk/getperson.php?personID=I13328&tree=2
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LJRP-F2P
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yuri_I_of_Galicia
2 CONT
2 CONT Yuri I of Galicia (born April 24, 1252 (1257?) – March 18, 1308) was prince of Belz (1264–1301) and King of Galicia-Volhynia or King of Rus' (1301–1308).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a son of Lev Daniilovich (Knyaz of Galich, 1269–1301) and Constance of Hungary, a daughter of King Béla IV and Maria Laskarina.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married three times. His first wife was Yaroslavna of Tver (died ca. 1286). His second wife was Euphemia of Kuyavia (died 18 March 1308), daughter of Casimir I of Kuyavia, who in turn was the son of Konrad of Masovia, Kuyavia, 
2 CONC Łęczyca, and Sieradz.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Mikhail (1283–1286) (first marriage)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Andrew of Galicia, Prince of Galicia-Volhynia (1308–1323)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Lev II, Prince of Lutsk (1308–1323)
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughters
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Maria, Princess of Halych-Lviv, (died January 11, 1341). Married Trojden I of Masovia
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Anastasia (parentage uncertain; died 1364–1365). Married Alexander I of Tver (died 1339)
2 CONT
