1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Gleb Vladimirovich''' (d. 1219) - specific prince of Ryazan.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1195 he was present in Vladimir at the wedding of Konstantin Vsevolodovich.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1196, holding the side of his father-in-law, Davyd Rostislavich prince of Smolensk, Gleb participated in the war with the Olgoviches of Chernigov and barely escaped captivity.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1207 together with his brother Oleg, he accused his uncles, Roman and Svyatoslav Glebovich, of treason to the Grand Duke Vsevolod the Big Nest, which caused their imprisonment, two Svyatoslavichs, Ingvar and Yuri Igorevich.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ryazan reign was given to Prince Yaroslav Vsevolodovich of Vladimir, and the Principality of Pronsk to Oleg Vladimirovich, for joint use with Gleb. This was not enough for Gleb, and in 1209 he decided to annex Ryazan to his po
2 CONC ssessions. However, this venture failed.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Congress in Isady'''
2 CONT
2 CONT On July 20, 1217, Gleb and his brother Constantine organized a princely congress in Isady, according to V. N. Tatishchev, to distribute inheritances after the death of Roman Glebovich, who died in captivity in Vladimir (1216).
2 CONT
2 CONT Gleb and Constantine, with the help of the Polovtsians (Cumans), organized at the congress the murder of their own brother Izyaslav and five cousins, including Roman Igorevich. After the death of Roman, the Ryazan reign was occupi
2 CONC ed by his brother Ingvar, who was not at the congress. In 1219 Ingvar defeated Gleb and the Polovtsians (Cumans), then, asking for help from the Grand Duke of Vladimir Yuri Vsevolodovich, defeated them again.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gleb fled to the Polovtsians (Cumans), where he soon died, having gone mad.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Vladimir Glebovich (d. 1186) - Pronsky prince (1180-?).
2 CONT
2 CONT Brothers:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Oleg (died before 1217) - prince of Pronsk (1208-until 1217).
2 CONT * Constantine (died after 1241) - prince of Pronsk (1208-1217).
2 CONT * Izyaslav (killed 1217) - prince of Pronsk (1207), principal prince of Pronsk (1208-1217).
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: daughter of the Smolensk prince Davyd Rostislavich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gleb Vladimirovich left no offspring - no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In culture'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In the novel "Batu" by Vasily Yan, a fictional story is given that Gleb Vladimirovich was expelled by the Ryazan  and became a scout for khan Batu during his campaign in North-Eastern Rus', and after the completion of the campaign
2 CONC , khan Batu refused to make him a Baskak in Ryazan and escorted him to the steppe where the prince went mad.
