2 CONC x thousandth cavalry, which was supposed to cut the main forces of the Tatars at the decisive moment of the battle. The idea of ​​Grand Duke Olgerd completely worked: the cavalry attacked the Tatars from the flank and put them to 
2 CONC flight, and then pursued for several days to the mouth of the Danube. Mikhail Evnutevich also participated in the battle on Vorskla in 1399, but it ended in disaster for the Lithuanians, and Mikhail himself died.
