1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dmitry "the Elder" or Sr. (Dmitrijus "Algirdaitis" - LT), date of birth unknown - d. Aug. 12, 1399 - the locative prince of Bryansk, Starodubsk, and Trubchevo, allegedly from the Gediminids dynasty, the founder of 
2 CONC the Trubetskoy princes lineage. Son of Vasili Drutsky or Constantine Drutsky. Vassal of Grand Duke of Lithuania Algirdas. Alleged son of the Grand Duke of Lithuania Algirdas and princess of Vitebsk Maria Yaroslavna - he is not lis
2 CONC ted among 12 Algirdas' sons in the oldest genealogy source in the Vatican archive. Dmitry "the Elder" in the Battle of Kulikovo acted as an ally of Dmitry Ivanovich Donsky.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dmitry Sr., alleged son of Algirdas, (not to be confused with Algirdas' younger son Kaributas-Dmitry) since about 1370 was appointed prince of Bryansk and Starodubo, in the winter of 1379–1380 lost all his possessions due to trans
2 CONC fer to service of the Moscovian prince. After 1380, these same lands were transferred to Algirdas's son Dmitry-Kaributas.
2 CONT
2 CONT For most of his life, Dmitry Sr. fought with Algirdas' son Jogaila (Jagiello - PL) in alliance with the prince of Moscow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dmitry Sr. was appointed as a ruler Pereslavl-Zalessky. Dmitry was killed on August 12, 1399, in the battle of Vorskla (near Vorskla River) on the side of the Lithuanian army against the Tatars.
