1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.ancestryfootprints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/Polish-Royal-Ancestry-Book-2.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT Book 1 ended with Saint Hedwig (Jadwiga) Queen of Poland, who died without a heir. This
2 CONT
2 CONT Book 2 begins with her husband,
2 CONT
2 CONT  Jogaila Wladyslaw II Jagiello King of Poland, 
2 CONT
2 CONT and continues with his descendants by his second wife. He is not a direct ancestor for us but we have common
2 CONT ancestors. Two common lineages, one from Vladimir II "Monomach" Grand Duke of Kiev (26th
2 CONT great grand father), and the other from Erik X Knutsson King of Sweden (22nd great grand
2 CONT father) are listed and their descendants are described in this book
2 CONT
2 CONT ALGIRDAS [Olgierd], s/o GEDIMINAS Grand Duke of Lithuania & Olga Vsevolodovna of Smolensk]  ([1296]-end May 1377).  Baptised ALEKSANDER.  
2 CONT x  (1318) [MARIA] Iaroslavna of Vitebsk, d/o IAROSLAV Vasilievich Prince of Vitebsk (-1346). 
2 CONT >1.         ANDREI 
2 CONT >2.         KONSTANTIN 
2 CONT >3.         OLEŁKO WŁODZIMIERZ 
2 CONT >4.         FEODOR 
2 CONT >5.       KORIBUTAS 
2 CONT >6.         FEODORA
2 CONT >7.         daughter 
2 CONT >8.         MARIA [Agrafena]
2 CONT
2 CONT xx ([1350]) IULIANA Aleksandrovna of Tver, d/o ALEXANDER I Mikhailovich Prince of Tver, ex-Grand Prince of Vladimir & Anastasia [Iurievna of Galich] ([1325]-1392). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >9.         KENNA ([1350]-27 Apr 1368). 
2 CONT >10.      '''>JOGAILA [Jagiello] Grand Duke of Lithuania, son of ALGIRDAS [Olgierd] Grand Duke of Lithuania & his second wife Iuliana Aleksandrovna of Tver [Rurikid] ([1351]-Grodek 31 May 1434, bur Krakow Cathedral).  Prince of Ki
2 CONC ev 1377.  He supported the Tatar Khan Mamai against Dmitry Ivanovich Prince of Moscow, Grand Prince of Vladimir, although his forces failed to arrive in time to help the Khan at the battle of Kulikovo in 1380[647].  Grand Duke of 
2 CONC Lithuania 1382/3-1386 and 1392/1401.  He was baptised at Krakow in Feb 1386 as WŁADYSŁAW, shortly before his first marriage, at which time he was recognised as WŁADISŁAW II King of Poland.'''
2 CONT >m firstly (18 Feb 1386) JADVIGA of Hungary King (rex) of Poland, daughter of LAJOS I King of Hungary [LUDWIK King of Poland] & his second wife Jelisaveta Kotromanić of Bosnia (Krakow 18 Feb 1373-Krakow 12 Jun 1400, bur Krakow, Ca
2 CONC thedral St Stanislas).  Her mother installed her as King (rex) of Poland in 1384, contrary to the last wishes of her father who wished to maintain the unity of the two crowns.  She was crowned at Krakow 15 Oct 1384.  The Catalogus
2 CONC  abbatum Sanganensium records that "filia minor regis Ungarorum" was betrothed to "duci Austrie" but later married "Poloni…duci…Vladislao vel Wolislao" but that the marriage was childless[648].  She won Galicia and Silesia back fr
2 CONC om Hungary.  She died in childbirth.  The procedure for her beatification was opened at Krakow 22 Apr 1949 by Prince Cardinal Sapieha, Archbishop of Krakow. King Władisław & his first wife had one child:
2 CONT >>1.         ELŹBIETA BONIFACIA (22 Jun 1399-13 Jul 1399). 
2 CONT >m secondly (Krakow 29 Jan 1401) ANNA of Celje, daughter of WILHELM Graf von Cilly & his wife Anna of Poland [Piast] ([1380/81]-[20/21] Mar 1416). King Władisław & his second wife had one child:
2 CONT >>2.         JADWIGA (8 Apr 1408-8 Dec 1431). 
2 CONT >m thirdly (2 May 1417) as her fourth husband, ELŹBIETA Pilcka, widow firstly of WYSZLE Czemborg, secondly of JANCZYK Janczykowicz Hiczyński and thirdly of WINCENTY Granowski castellan of Nakel, daughter of OTTO Pilcka, Voivode of
2 CONC  Sandomir ([1372]-12 May 1420). 
2 CONT >m fourthly (1420) SOFIA Ivanovna of Kiev, daughter of IVAN Borisovich Prince of Kiev . 
2 CONT >m fifthly (7 Feb 1422) ZOFIA [Sonka] Holczańska, daughter of ANDRZEJ Ivanovich Prince of Kiev & his wife Alexandra Dmitrievna of Druck ([1405]-21 Sep 1461). King Władisław & his fifth wife had three children:
2 CONT >>3.         WŁADISŁAW (31 Oct 1424-killed in battle Varna 10 Nov 1444).  He succeeded his father in 1434 as WŁADISŁAW III “Warneczyk” King of Poland.  He was elected ULÁSZLÓ I King of Hungary by a council of Nobles at Buda in ear
2 CONC ly 1440, before the birth of Ladislas [László] "Posthumous" Archduke of Austria, posthumous son of his predecessor Albrecht Duke of Austria, King of Hungary and Bohemia.  After his arrival in Buda, he was recognised as king by mos
2 CONC t of László's supporters.  The resulting civil war was mediated by the church, which resulted in the acceptance of the King of Poland as king.  A papally sponsored Hungarian/Serb led crusade in 1443 recaptured Smederovo, Niš and S
2 CONC ofija, but was turned back at Adrianople.  Sultan Murad II negotiated peace terms under which he agreed to the restoration of the Serb state and a ten-year truce[649].  The Pope encouraged King Władisław to launch a second crusade
2 CONC  the following year, in which Serbia refused to participate, in defiance of the agreed truce, but he was defeated and killed in battle by Sultan Murad at Varna 10 Nov 1444.
2 CONT >>4.         KAZIMIERZ (16 May 1426-2 Mar 1427).
2 CONT >>5.         KAZIMIERZ (30 Nov 1427-Grodno 7 Jun 1492, bur Krakow Cathedral).  He was chosen to succeed in 1440 as Grand Duke of Lithuania after the murder of Grand Duke Korybut[650].  He succeeded his brother in 1444 as KAZIMIERZ
2 CONC  IV "the Great" King of Poland.  He claimed ecclesiastical jurisdiction over Kiev and all the Rus lands, challenging the authority of Metropolitan Iona in Moscow and seeking the allegiance of the Orthodox princes of western Rus.  
2 CONC He gave refuge to many dissidents from the Riurikid dynasty, in particular Dmitry Iurievich "Shemiakha" who briefly succeeded as Grand Prince of Vladimir in 1446.  In 1480, a group of dissidents led by Prince Fedor Ivanovich Belsk
2 CONC y rebelled unsuccessfully against Kasimierz in Lithuania.  Belsky fled to Moscow in 1481, from where he continually raided the Lithuanian borders[651].  m (Krakow 10 Feb 1454) ELISABETH Archduchess of Austria, daughter of ALBRECHT
2 CONC  V Duke of Austria [ALBRECHT II King of the Romans, ALBERT King of Hungary, and ALBRECHT King of Bohemia] & his wife Elisabeth Pss of Bohemia and Hungary [Luxembourg] ([1435/36]-30 Aug 1505, bur Krakow Cathedral).  The Catalogus a
2 CONC bbatum Sanganensium records that one daughter of "Albertus dux Austrie" married "Kazimiro regi Polonie"[652].   https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/POLAND.htm#WladislawIIdied1434
