1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Skirgaila (Belarusian: Скіргайла), also known as Ivan, also known as Casimir
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: ca. 1353 or 1354 Died: 11 January 1397 in Kiev;  Baptized 1383/1384 as Casimir 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Algirdas Mother: Uliana of Tver
2 CONT
2 CONT Skirgaila was a regent of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania for his brother Jogaila from 1386 to 1392. He was son of Algirdas, Grand Duke of Lithuania, and his second wife Uliana of Tver.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Algirdas' death in 1377, Jogaila became the Grand Duke. It is believed that dynastic disputes that soon erupted between him and his uncle Kęstutis and his cousin Vytautas the Great were largely inspired by Skirgaila. It is k
2 CONC nown about his travels to the Teutonic Knights in 1379 just a year prior to the controversial Treaty of Dovydiškės. Skirgaila was the chief supporter of his brother Jogaila and helped him to imprison both Kęstutis and Vytautas in 
2 CONC Kreva castle during the Lithuanian Civil War (1381–1384). Some historians speculate that Kęstutis' death after a week in prison was in fact assassination carried out by Skirgaila. As a reward for a job well done, Skirgaila receive
2 CONC d the Duchy of Trakai. When Jogaila was preparing for the Union of Kreva, Skirgaila was actively involved in the negotiations and even headed a diplomatic mission to Poland. The negotiations succeeded and Jogaila married Jadwiga o
2 CONC f Poland and was crowned as King of Poland in 1386. He left Skirgaila as his regent in Lithuania. However, Skirgaila was not popular with the nobles and Vytautas saw this as an opportunity to gain power. In 1389 he started a new c
2 CONC ivil war, but after an unsuccessful attack on Vilnius he had to seek help from the Teutonic Knights. In 1392 Jogaila and Vytautas signed Ostrów Agreement, and Vytautas became his regent of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania. The Duchy o
2 CONC f Trakai was returned to Vytautas as his patrimony. As a compensation Skirgaila received a portion of Volhynia and Kiev since 1395. The circumstances surrounding his death are not entirely clear. It is rumored he was poisoned by t
2 CONC he order of Orthodox Church officials. He was interred in Kiev Pechersk Lavra.
2 CONT
2 CONT Skirgaila (apie 1354-1397 m. sausio 11 d. Kijeve), Trakų kunigaikštis 1382-1395 m., Kijevo kunigaikštis (1395-1397 m.), Lietuvos regentas;
2 CONT
2 CONT Skirgaila (1383 ar 1384 m. apsikrikštijęs pagal katalikiškas apeigas gavo vardą Kazimieras, valdydamas Kijevą nuo 1395 m. vadinosi stačiatikišku vardu Ivanas, apie 1353 m. – 1397 m. sausio 11 d.) – lietuvių kunigaikštis. Lietuvos 
2 CONC didžiojo kunigaikščio Algirdo ir jo antrosios žmonos Julijonos sūnus. Buvo ūmaus būdo, garsėjo kaip mėgėjas išgerti. 1379 m. Skirgaila savo brolio Jogailos pavedimu lankėsi įvairiose Europos šalyse, informuodamas jų valdovus apie 
2 CONC Jogailos ir kt. Algirdaičių apsisprendimą atsiversti į katalikybę. 1382 m. padėjęs Jogailai susigrąžinti iš Kęstučio 1381 m. prarastą valdžią (dalis istorikų mano, kad Kęstutis 1382 m. buvo nužudytas būtent Skirgailos nurodymu), S
2 CONC kirgaila už tai gavo Trakų ir Polocko kunigaikštystes (Trakus valdė 1382–1392, Polocką – 1386 – 1393 m.), o 1386 m. (oficialiai – 1387 m. balandį) – ir Lietuvos didžiojo kunigaikščio vietininko Lietuvoje pareigas. 1385 m. vadovavo
2 CONC  Jogailos atstovų deryboms su lenkų didikais dėl Jogailos ir Jadvygos vedybų bei Jogailos vainikavimo Lenkijos karaliumi. 1392 m. vasarą Jogailai savo vietininku Lietuvoje paskyrus Vytautą, Skirgaila kurį laiką liko tik Polocko ku
2 CONC nigaikščiu. Vėliau (1393(?) – 1395 m.) jis valdė dalį Volynės, o nuo 1395 m. – Kijevo kunigaikštystę. Mirė Kijeve nunuodytas lietuviškosios Rusios stačiatikių hierarchų nurodymu (?) ar apsinuodijęs alkoholiu. Palaidotas Kijevo Peč
2 CONC iorų vienuolyne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Skirgiełło Iwan (z drugiego; †11.I.1397); ks. trocki 1382, połocki 1387, kijowski 1395, namiestnik na Litwie 1386-1392, chrzest w obrządku wschodnim 1383/1384
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ALGIRDAS [Olgierd], s/o GEDIMINAS Grand Duke of Lithuania & Olga Vsevolodovna of Smolensk]  ([1296]-end May 1377).  Baptised ALEKSANDER.  
2 CONT x  (1318) [MARIA] Iaroslavna of Vitebsk, d/o IAROSLAV Vasilievich Prince of Vitebsk (-1346). 
2 CONT >1.         ANDREI 
2 CONT >2.         KONSTANTIN 
2 CONT >3.         OLEŁKO WŁODZIMIERZ 
2 CONT >4.         FEODOR 
2 CONT >5.       KORIBUTAS 
2 CONT >6.         FEODORA
2 CONT >7.         daughter 
2 CONT >8.         MARIA [Agrafena]
2 CONT
2 CONT xx ([1350]) IULIANA Aleksandrovna of Tver, d/o ALEXANDER I Mikhailovich Prince of Tver, ex-Grand Prince of Vladimir & Anastasia [Iurievna of Galich] ([1325]-1392). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >9.         KENNA   
2 CONT
2 CONT >10.      JOGAILA [Jagiello] 
2 CONT >11.      '''SKIRGAILA [Skirgajllo] (-11 Jan 1397).  The Origo Regis Jagyelo records that "dux Jagello" granted "Poloczko" to "fratri suo Sergallo"[117].  He was baptised IVAN in [1383/84].  Prince of Troik 1382.  Prince of Polock
2 CONC  1387.  "Schirgalo…dux Lithuanie et dominus Tracensis et Polocensis" confirmed peace with the Teutonic Order by charter dated 1388, sealed by "domini Alexandri ducis Lithwanie et domini Kernoviensis"[118].  Prince of Kiev 1395.  P
2 CONC rince of Lithuania 1386-1392.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >12.      LENGVENIS
2 CONT
2 CONT >13.      KORIGAILA [Korigajllo] (-killed in battle Vilna 28 Oct 1392).  He was baptised KAZIMIERZ in 1386.
2 CONT
2 CONT >14.      WIGAND
2 CONT >15.      ŠVITRIGAILA 
2 CONT >16.      ELENA 
2 CONT
2 CONT >17.      MARIA 
2 CONT
2 CONT >18.      WILHEIDA KATARZYNA 
2 CONT >19.      ALEKSANDRA 
2 CONT
2 CONT >20.      JADWIGA 
2 CONT
