2 CONT
2 CONT Literature
2 CONT
2 CONT Rowell S. C. Lithuania Ascending: The Pagan Empire in East-Central Europe, 1295-1345. - Cambridge University Press, 1994.
2 CONT Puzyna J., which priest Giedymina called and really called Pukuwer // Vilnius Ateneum. v.10. 1935. pp. 1-43.
2 CONT Gudavičius E. The so-called "Diarchy" in the Grand Duchy of Lithuania // Feodalisms Baltijas regiona, Riga, 1985, pp. 35-44.
2 CONT Peter of Dusburg. Chronicle of the Prussian Land. Mr. Ladomir. 1997.
2 CONT Nasevich, VL The Beginnings of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania: Events and Personalities / V.L. Nasiewicz. - Minsk: Polymya, 1993. - 160 p.
2 CONT Petrauskas, R. Lithuanian nobility at the end of the 14th - 15th centuries: Composition - structure - power / R. Petrauskas; alley. from Lithuanian. the languages ​​of A. Mikus. - Smolensk: Inbelkult, 2014.- 386 p.
2 CONT Belarusian encyclopedia: In 18 volumes / Ed .: GP Pashkov et al. - Mn .: BelEn, 1996. - Vol. 3: Belarusians - Woraniec. - 511 points - 10,000 copies. - ISBN 985-11-0068-4 (vol. 3), ISBN 985-11-0035-8. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Butygejd (Budikid; Belarusian: Будзікід) was the Grand Duke of Lithuania from 1285 to 1291. He is the first known and undisputed member of the Gediminids.
2 CONT
2 CONT He started his rule when the Livonian Order and the Teutonic Knights were finalizing their conquest of the Baltic tribes. In 1289, leading about 8,000 troops, Butigeidis attacked Sambia. In 1289 the Teutonic Knights built a castle
2 CONC  in Tilsit and their raids intensified. Lithuanians were forced to abandon Koklainiai Castle located on the other bank of the river. Butigeidis was the first to build strong castles along the Neman River. The castle system was fur
2 CONC ther developed after his death and helped to resist the raids until the second half of the 14th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Butigeidis transferred Vaŭkavysk to Galicia-Volhynia in exchange for peace. He died in 1290 or 1292, and his brother Butvydas (also known as Pukuveras) inherited the crown.
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butigeidis
