1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Jerzy Giedygołd Kojlikinowicz''' of the Leliwa coat of arms '' (died after June 9, 1435) - member of the ruling council of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania in 1411-1431, Vilnius voivode in the years 1425-1432, Smole
2 CONC nsk governor around 1424, Podole starost in 1411- 1423, Kiev voivode before February 1, 1411, marshal in 1401.
2 CONT
2 CONT Moniwid's brother. A supporter of Świdrygiełło, after the defeat of Oszmiana in the captivity of Zygmunt Kiejstutowicz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography
2 CONT
2 CONT Lidia Korczak, Lithuanian Grand Ducal Council in the 15th Century, Kraków 1998, p. 83.
2 CONT Central officials and dignitaries of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania in the 14th-18th centuries. Lists. Compiled by Henryk Lulewicz and Andrzej Rachuba. Kórnik 1994, p. 207. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hedigold (in Jury Catholicism;? - until June 9, 1435) - statesman of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania. Voivode of Kiev (1411), deputy of Smolensk (about 1424), voivode of Vilnius (1426-1432).
2 CONT
2 CONT He owned the estates of Vishnev, Volma, Dzeraunaya, Kamen, Nalibaki, Radashkovichi in Minsk district, Mir and Sverzhan in Navahrudak district [1]; from Sigismund Kistutovich received the estate of Vishnev in Ashmiany district. He 
2 CONC held the Podolsk fort (1411—1423).
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT From the Lithuanian boyar family, son of Kailikin (Gailigin). He had a brother, Wojciech Maniwid. During the formation of the Horadle Union (1413) he adopted the coat of arms "Laliva".
2 CONT
2 CONT First mentioned in 1401 as the court marshal Vytautas. He signed as a witness the act of the Vilnius-Radom Union (1401), the Peace of Toruń (1411). In 1415 he went to the Council of Constantinople (1414-1418). In 1429 he was ambas
2 CONC sador to Jagiello in the coronation of Vytautas with the royal crown.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the feudal war (1431-1435) he first supported Svidrigail. When the latter was assassinated in Ashmiany (1432), he was among the small detachment with which Svidrigail fled to Polotsk. In the battle of Ashmiany on December 8
2 CONC , 1432 he was taken prisoner by Sigismund Kistutovich. Then he got rid of the voivodship government. He later acknowledged Sigismund's authority and testified in his documents as a lord of Vyshneve until 1435. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He had a son Senka.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Pozdnyakov V. Hedigold // GDL. Encyclical. Vol. 1. - Minsk, 2005. S. 522.
2 CONT ^ Pozdnyakov V. Hedigold // GDL. Encyclical. Vol. 1. - Minsk, 2005. S. 521.
2 CONT ^ Code of Diplomatic Chair and Diocese of Vilnius. No. 139. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Literature 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Grand Duchy of Lithuania: Encyclopedia. In 3 vols. / Ed. GP Pashkov et al. Volume 2: Cadet Corps - Yatskevich. - Minsk: Belarusian Encyclopedia, 2005. - 788 pp .: ill. ISBN 985-11-0378-0.
2 CONT * Semkowicz W. O litewskich rodach bojarskich zbratanych ze szlachtą polska v Horodle r.1413 // Miesięcznik Heraldyczny. Organ of the Heraldic Society in Lviv. R. 6. Nr 11—12. 1913 
2 CONT * W.Semkowicz. O litewskich rodach bojarskich zbratanych ze szlachtą polską w Horodle r.1413. Miesięcznik Heraldyczny. Organ Towarzystwa Heraldycznego we Lwowie. R.6 1913 nr11-12 
