1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT duke Patrikas of Korela/Karelia, lord over the fifth of Vadja, castellan of Kaprio, Pähkinälinna, Käkisalmi, etc (b est 1340; d aft 1408)
2 CONT
2 CONT his (younger) son: duke Jyrki of Korela/Karelia, Juri Patrikanpoika (fl 1408; d aft perhaps 1447; b est 1380s)
2 CONT
2 CONT his elder son: duke Vasle Jurinpoika, prince Patrikeiev (b est 1410s; d 1450) - or 'Vasili Jurievich'
2 CONT
2 CONT his son: duke Iivana Vaslenpoika 'bulgak' (d 1498; b est 1440s) - or, 'Ivan Vasilievich'
2 CONT
2 CONT his son: duke Mikael Iivananpoika 'golitsa' (d 1554; b bef est 1470) - or: 'Mikhail Ivanovich'
2 CONT
2 CONT his son: duke Juri Mikaelinpoika Bulgakov-Galitsin (d 1560; b est 1490s) - or: 'Juri Mikhailovich'
2 CONT
2 CONT his son: duke Iivana Jurinpoika Bulgakov-Galitsin (d 1583; b est 1520) - or: 'Ivan Jurievich'
2 CONT
2 CONT his daughter: princess Elena Iivanantytär Galitsin (b est 1540s); married boyar Grigori Mikhailovich Aminev, butler of Muscovia
2 CONT
2 CONT - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - and here, we deal with ascertained residents of (Finnish-speaking) Ingria
2 CONT
2 CONT their son: boyar Teuvo Reijonpoika Aminev, 1.Lord of Gluhova, Obskova and Pihkovitsa, castellan of Jaanilidna and Oudova (fl 1610; d 1628; b est 1560), naturalized nobleman in peerage of Sweden as soon as Ingria got incorporated; 
2 CONC Jaanilidna = in russian: Ivangorod, in Ingria; 'Feudor Reijonpoika/Rekonpoika/Grigorievich'
2 CONT * he has a lot of descendants, quite much in Finland
2 CONT
2 CONT for example, his son: boyar Teppana Teuvonpoika Aminev, 2.Lord of Gluhova (fl 1612; d bef 1649; b est 1580s)
2 CONT
2 CONT his son: cavalry captain Reittu Teppananpoika Aminev (slain 1656; b est 1620s), 'Fredrik', 'Feudor Teppananpoika'; married Anna Elisabet Armfeldt (d aft 1678)
2 CONT
2 CONT his son: cavalry captain Juhana Reittu Aminoff (b est 1650); married Elisabet Güntersberch
2 CONT
2 CONT their daughters included: Loviisa Aminoff (b 1685; d 1741), married baron Kaarle Kustaa Armfeldt (b 1666; d 1736)
