1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bohdan Semenovich Sapieha (c. 1450 - c. 1512) was a court secretary of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania, Okolnichy of Smolensk, and one of the early builders of the future prominence of the Sapieha family of the Lis co
2 CONC at of arms. He was the eldest son of Semen Sapieha.
2 CONT He served Grand Duke Casimir Jagiellon and is recorded as a state secretary between 1471 and 1488. Through his marriage to Princess Teodora (Fedia) Sokolinska of the Drutsk princely family, he considerably expanded the family’s la
2 CONC nded possessions.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1504 and 1507 he took part in diplomatic missions to Moscow. During one of these embassies he was held hostage and spent about a year in captivity before being released through the intervention of Grand Duke Sigismund I the Old
2 CONC .
2 CONT He died around 1512 and is regarded as the progenitor of the Ruzhany–Cheryea branch of the House of Sapieha.
