1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ARMENIA.htm#ZampeaMManuelPalailogosKantakuzenos
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         ZAMPEA [Isabelle] de Lusignan (1333-[1382/87], bur Mistra).  Kantakuzenus records the betrothal of "imperatore, Manueli filio" and "Syrgem Ntelensuziam, imperatoris Andronici consobrinum, Cypriorum regis filium…filiam",
2 CONC  in a passage dated to [1341], the same source recording in a later passage that "Syrgen" terminated the betrothal after learning of Manuel's betrothal in 1342 to "Liberi filiam"[874].  The Chronicle of Jean Dardel names "madame Y
2 CONC sabel de Lisegnan, fille du…roy Guy d'Armenye", when recording that Pierre I King of Cyprus met her at "Moudon"[875].  She was known as MARIA or MARGARETA in Greece.  Referred to as "sole heir of the late Prince of Tyre" by her gr
2 CONC andfather in the letter of Pope Clement VI dated 30 Jun 1347 addressed to the king of Cyprus which requested him to give her back her estates in Cyprus, which Rüdt-Collenberg highlights as proof of the illegitimacy of all other de
2 CONC scendants of Amaury de Lusignan then living, including that of the future Lewon V King of Armenia[876].  The Chronicle of Amadi records that "madama Margarita de Lusignan, nezza del signor de Sur et sorella del re Livon de Armenia
2 CONC , relitta del quondam Manoel Catacusino despotto della Morea" came to Cyprus in 1372[877].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (betrothed [1341], after 26 Feb 1349) MANUEL Palaiologos Kantakuzenos, son of Emperor IOANNES VI & his wife Eirene Asanina (-1380).  Governor of the Peloponese. 
