1 NOTE John or Ivan I of the western provinces of Bulgaria was assassinated by Ivanko a Boyar of Bulgaria in 1195, who then took over command of the western provinces.  Ivanko ruled until 1197, and lost to the younger Asen brother, Kaloy
2 CONC an.
2 CONT
2 CONT John I or Ivan of Asen, with his brother, Peter, led a revolt against the Byzantines, and formed an independent state of Bulgaria about 1183.  The Agents of the Byzantines from Constantinople were using extortion, which led to the
2 CONC  revolt.   The Asen brothers, who are Boyars, gained the support of the Cumans against the Byzatine Empire of Isaac II Angelus.
