1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_I_Orsini
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://www.genmarenostrum.com/pagine-lettere/letterao/Orsini/ORSINI-EPIRO.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT   B1. (ex1°) Giovanni I (+ ca. 1317), 
2 CONT
2 CONT Conte Palatino dal 1304, Signore di Leucade dal 1295, Consignore di Cefalonia e  Zante dal 1303.
2 CONT
2 CONT        = 1292 Maria Angela, figlia di Tommaso I Despota d’Epiro e di Anna Paleologa Cantacuzena (nipote  dell’Imperatore Michele VIII) (+ post 1304).
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LATIN%20LORDSHIPS%20IN%20GREECE.htm#GiovanniOrsinidied1317
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         GIOVANNI Orsini (-1317).  The Livre de la Conqueste de la Morée names “messire Jehan de Cephalonie” as oldest son of “le conte Richart de Cephalonie”[644].  Lord of Leukas 1295.  He succeeded his father in 1304 as Count
2 CONC  of Kefalonia.  “Jehan, comte palatins, sire de Chephalonie et de Jachint” issued a charter dated 7 Apr 1304 relating to his inheritance in which he names “madame Marie Comnene nostre comtesse…et leal espose”[645].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ([1293]) MARIA Komnene Dukaina Angelina, daughter of NIKEPHOROS Dukas Angelos Lord of Epirus & his second wife Anna Palaiologina Kantakuzene.  The Livre de la Conqueste de la Morée refers to “la dame dou conte Jehan” as “l
2 CONC e despot…sa fille”, the marriage being dated to [1293] from the context of a later passage[646].  “Jehan, comte palatins, sire de Chephalonie et de Jachint” issued a charter dated 7 Apr 1304 relating to his inheritance in which he
2 CONC  names “madame Marie Comnene nostre comtesse…et leal espose”[647].  Her marriage was arranged as a reward for her future father-in-law helping her father expel the Byzantines from Epirus in [1292][648].  Count Giovanni & his wife 
2 CONC had four children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT nemesi előneve: kephalloniai, palota báró és arkón ( Count Palatine/ Archon)
