1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Roman Ingvarevich''' (d. January 1238) - one of the sons of the Ryazan prince Ingvar Igorevich, who died in 1235. He is considered the younger brother of Yuri of Ryazan and the Kolomna prince during the Mongol i
2 CONC nvasion.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Resurrection Chronicle under 1217, when listing the sons of Ingvar, he stands before Yuri and Oleg. In the primary sources, he is not mentioned as the Kolomna prince. For example, the Novgorod chronicle reports that Yuri wa
2 CONC s under siege in Ryazan, and Roman "began to fight with his people." The association of Roman with Kolomna is primarily due to the Battle of Kolomna, where he, together with the Vladimir army, met the Mongols. Voitovich identifies
2 CONC  it with the mentioned "The Tale of the Devastation of Ryazan by Batu" Gleb Ingvarevich Kolomensky.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roman and Yeremey Glebovich, the governor of Vladimir, went under siege in Kolomna, and the Vladimir prince Vsevolod also participated in the battle, whom his father sent to help the Ryazan princes with all the people. In the batt
2 CONC le, Roman and the voivode Yeremey, as well as the youngest son of Genghis Khan Kulkan, were killed. Vsevolod with the remnants of the troops managed to return to Vladimir.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Mongolian court chronicler Rashid ad-Din, of all the defenders of Rus', pays the most attention to Roman and, possibly, ascribes to the future Mongol Khan Munk participation in the campaign to the north and in the battle of Ko
2 CONC lomna.
2 CONT
2 CONT Researchers of the Mongol invasion of Rus' Khrapachevsky R.P. and Kargalov V.V. mistakenly call Roman Igorevich (Roman Igorevich died at the princely congress in 1217).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince of Riazanj ( 1213- 1217 ). 
