1 NAME Gertrude /von Comburg/
2 GIVN Gertrude
2 SURN von Comburg
1 SEX F
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 1130 AND 1131
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} rom Wikipedia,<br/>
2 CONT <br/>Gertrude of Comburg (died 1130/1131) was the first queen consort of Conrad III of Germany. She was a daughter of Henry, Count of Rothenburg, and Gepa of Mergentheim.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her marriage to Conrad of Swabia is estimated to have occurred c. 1115. Her new husband was the second son of Frederick I, Duke of Swabia and Agnes of Germany. He was a younger brother of Frederick II, Duke of Swabia.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1115, Conrad was appointed Duke of Franconia by his maternal uncle Henry V, Holy Roman Emperor. Henry V died on 23 May 1125 and Conrad was an eligible candidate for the throne. However, Conrad supported his older brother Freder
2 CONC ick II in the election for the new King of the Romans. The election was instead won by Lothair III.
2 CONT
2 CONT Conrad and Frederick II had inherited the private lands of their deceased maternal uncle Henry V but also pressed a claim to lands gained by the crown during his reign. Lothair III also claimed the lands as the new King. Their con
2 CONC flict resulted in Conrad being elected King of Germany in opposition to Lothair in 1127. Gertrud became his Queen consort. The conflict was still ongoing at the time of her death.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Gertrud and Conrad III had at least two daughters whose names are known: Bertha (recorded as abbess of Erstein in 1153) and Gertrud.[1] Another daughter (probably named Agnes), who died in 1151, married Iziaslav II of Kie
2 CONC v.[2]<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Conrad III had other children: two by his second wife Gertrude of Sulzbach (Heinrich-Berengar and Friedrich IV of Swabia) and five with a mistress called Gerberga (Leopold, Konstantin von Lochgarten, Giselbert von Hotingen, Sophia
2 CONC , who married Konrad von Pfitzingen, and Ludmilla von Vellberg).<br/>
2 CONT <br/>Referens<br/>
2 CONT ^ a b Cawley, Charles, KONRAD III 1138-1152, Medieval Lands database, Foundation for Medieval Genealogy,[self-published source][better source needed] in Cawley, Charles, Medieval Lands: A prosopography of medieval European noble a
2 CONC nd royal families.<br/>
2 CONT ^ a b Marek, Miroslav. "A listing of descendants of Frederick I, Duke of Swabia". Genealogy.EU.[self-published source][better source needed]
