1 OCCU Comte, de Berg-Schalkingen, Greve av Berg-Schelklingen, Graf, stirbt als Mönch; Busse, DFA57. H. 1., Graf v.Berg um 1100, Mönch in Zwiefalten; v.Damm, Count of Berg-Schelklingen, Greve
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Heinrich Graf von Berg-Schelklingen''' was born circa 1073 in Schelklingen, Alb-Donau-Kreis, Baden-Württemberg, Germany. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-38474969 Poppo (1055~1090) Graf von Roggenstein und Berg] a
2 CONC nd [https://www.geni.com/profile-119505100 ÁRPÁD(házi) Sophia]. He was a Comte, de Berg-Schalkingen, Greve av Berg-Schelklingen, Graf, stirbt als Mönch; Busse, DFA57. H. 1., Graf v.Berg um 1100, Mönch in Zwiefalten; v.Damm, Count 
2 CONC of Berg-Schelklingen, Greve. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich married [https://www.geni.com/profile-26735094 Adelheid von Vohburg] in 1083. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-1792247 Salomea* von Berg-Schelklingen]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-21724124 Richza von Berg-Schelklingen]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-38476987 Diepold I von Berg-Schelklingen]; [https://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/profile-63353869 S Berg Schelkingen]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-81025679 Sophie von Berg- Schelklingen]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died circa September 24, 1122 in Zwiefalten, Reutlingen, Baden-Württemberg, Germany. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT *http://finnholbek.dk/getperson.php?personID=I26491&tree=2
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Berg-446 ''(abt. 1073 - bef. 1116)''
2 CONT --------
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/WURTTEMBERG.htm#HeinrichBergdiedbefore1116<br/>
2 CONT a)         HEINRICH [I] (-Zwiefalten 24 Sep before 1116, bur Zwiefalten).  Ortlieb's Chronicon of Zwiefalten names "Heinricus de Berge" as son of "Bobbonis comitis et Sophiæ ipsius uxori"[206].  Graf von Berg.  He became a monk at
2 CONC  Zwiefalten.  The necrology of Zwiefalten records the death "VIII Kal Oct" of "Heinricus com senior de Berge…sepultus in Capitolio...cum patre suo Poppone et fratribus suis" and his donation of “curiam Oppinthal”[207].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ADELHEID von Mochental, daughter of [DIEPOLD [II] von Giengen Markgraf im Nordgau & his wife Liutgarde von Zähringen] (-1 Dec [1125]).  The primary source which confirms her precise parentage has not yet been identified, a
2 CONC lthough the following necrology entry indicates her possible family origin.  It is, however, unusual for a deceased married lady to be referred to in contemporary necrologies with a comital title derived from her birth family.  It
2 CONC  is therefore possible that the reference to “Mochental” relates to an otherwise unrecorded second husband.  The necrology of Zwiefalten records the death "Kal Dec" of "Adelheit com de Mochintal et c v, mater Salome ducisse"[208].
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT  Heinrich & his wife had six children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://books.google.fi/books?id=cUdSAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA303&lpg=PA303&dq=Poppo+Graf+von+Berg-Schelklingen&source=bl&ots=QroVtqxfhl&sig=ux9felQGNk1nzmPYYPiT6pZml5g&hl=fi&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiLsq6Hp9zOAhWBO5oKHXmzBLw4FBDoAQgmMAE#v=onepage&q=
2 CONC Poppo%20Graf%20von%20Berg-Schelklingen&f=false
