1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sviatopolk married firstly a Bohemian princess (Přemyslid dynasty), probably a daughter of Duke Spytihněv II. They had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Zbyslava, married to king Boleslaw III of Poland on November 15, 1102.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Father:	fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands	SVIATOPOLK II /SVIATOPOLK MIKHAIL Iziaslavich
2 CONT
2 CONT 	thepeerage.com:		Svyatopolk I, Grand Duke of Kiev
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm#SviatopolkIIdied1113A
2 CONT
2 CONT SVIATOPOLK II 1093-1113
2 CONT
2 CONT SVIATOPOLK MIKHAIL Iziaslavich, son of IZIASLAV I Grand Prince of Kiev & his wife Gertrud of Poland (1050-16 Apr 1113). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly ---.  Baumgarten records this first marriage, citing a secondary source in support[214].  
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Grand Prince Sviatopolk II & his first wife had [four] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.             IAROSLAV Sviatopolkovich (-killed in battle May 1123).
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.             ZBISLAVA Sviatopolkovna (-[1109/12]).  The Primary Chronicle names Sbyslava, daughter of Svyatopolk when recording that she was taken to Poland 16 Nov 1102 to marry Boleslav[220].  The Chronica principum Polonie rec
2 CONC ords that the mother of "Boleslaus suo primogenito Wladislao filio" was "ex  quadam Ruthena nobili"[221].  m ([16 Nov 1102/early 1103]) as his first wife, BOLESŁAW III "Krzywousty/Wrymouth" King of Poland, son of WŁADYSŁAW I HERMA
2 CONC N Prince of Poland & his second wife Judith of Bohemia (20 Aug [1086]-28 Oct 1138).  
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.             ANNA Sviatopolkovna (-after 1136).
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.             PREDSLAVA Sviatopolkovna.  The Primary Chronicle names Predslava, daughter of Svyatopolk, when recording that she was taken to Hungary 21 Aug 1104 to marry the king's son[223].  Baumgarten names her husband as Álmos
2 CONC  but only cites one secondary source in support[224].  m (21 Aug 1104) ÁLMOS of Hungary, son of GÉZA I King of Hungary & his second wife --- Synadene ([1068]-1129).  He rebelled against his brother King Kálmán, declaring himself K
2 CONC ing of Hungary 1102-1109, but received little support.  He was blinded, together with his son, on the orders of his brother King Kálmán and fled to Constantinople[225].  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Zbyslawa of Kiev (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #114578, d. 1108
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=23 May 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT      Zbyslawa of Kiev was the daughter of Svyatopolk I, Grand Duke of Kiev and unknown daughter (?). (1), (2) She married Boleslaw III, Duke of Poland, son of Wladislaw I Herman, Duke of Poland and Judith of Bohemia, in 1103. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in 1108. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Zbyslawa of Kiev and Boleslaw III, Duke of Poland
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Wladislaw II, Duke of Poland+ b. 1105, d. 1159 (1)
2 CONT
