2 CONC en identified.  She is not one of Władysław's daughters referred to in the Chronicæ Polanorum[194].  The Fundatio Monasterii Richenbacensis names "Adelheidis" as wife of "marchio Dietpaldus" in connection with the foundation of Re
2 CONC ichenbach[195].  The necrology of Admont records the death "VIII Kal Mar" of "Adelheit marchyonissa"[196].  m ([before 1105]) as his first wife, DIETPOLD [III] Graf von Vohburg, Cham und Nabberg Markgraf der Nordgau, son of DIEPOL
2 CONC D [II] von Giengen Markgraf im Nordgau & his wife Liutgarde von Zähringen (-1146).] 
