1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uro%C5%A1_II_of_Rascia
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reign 1140-1161
2 CONT * Full name Uroš Urošević
2 CONT * Predecessor Uroš I of Rascia
2 CONT * Successor Desa of Serbia
2 CONT * Royal House House of Vukanović (Urošević)
2 CONT * Father Uroš I of Rascia
2 CONT * Religious beliefs † Eastern Orthodoxy
2 CONT
2 CONT Uroš II Urošević or Prvoslav (Primislav) (Serbian: Урош II Примислав) was a 12th-century Serbian Grand Prince of Rascia 1140-1150, 1152–1155, 1156-1161.
2 CONT
2 CONT Uroš II Primislav begins his rule of Rascia in 1140, and in 1149 he is attacked by the Byzantine Emperor Manuel I. His brother Beloš, palatine of the Kingdom of Hungary, and nephew Géza II, King of Hungary, aids him against the at
2 CONC tacks of Manuel I.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1150 Uroš II gives oaths to servitude to the Emperor,[1] Uroš instates Desa Urošević as co-ruler after he had gained Duklja and Travunia in 1148 (Serbian Primorje).[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1153 a dispute between the two brothers result in Desa ousting Uroš II. Byzantine Emperor Manuel I intervenes and re-instates Uroš II in 1155.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1161[1]-1162 the Byzantines removed him as the Grand Zhupan of Serbia, and his brother Beloš briefly ruled before Desa took the throne.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT *Ancestors of Uroš II Prvoslav
2 CONT **2 Father Uroš I of Rascia
2 CONT **3 Mother Anna Diogenissa
2 CONT **4 p.g.father Vukan of Rascia
2 CONT **6 m.g.father Ioannis Komnenos
2 CONT **7 m.g.mother  Anna Dalassena
