0 @N6000000004533196325@ NOTE From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Mstislav II Izyaslavich (???????? ????????? in Russian) (? - 1170),Prince of Pereyaslavl, Volynsk and Grand Prince of Kiev (1167-1169,1170). Son of Izyaslav Mstislavich, Grand Prince of Kiev.
0 @N6000000002187837180@ NOTE Mstislav II of Kiev
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Mstislav II Izyaslavich (???????? ????????? in Russian) (? - 1170), Kniaz' (Prince) of Pereyaslav, Volodymyr-Volynsky and Velikiy Kniaz (Grand Prince) of Kiev (1167-1169, 1170). Son of Izyaslav Mstislavich, Velikiy Kniaz' (Grand P
1 CONC rince) of Kiev.
1 CONT
1 CONT Along with his father, he participated in the wars against Yury Dolgoruky and the Chernigov princes. After an initial victory against the Cumans in 1153, Mstislav was defeated by the Cumans at the Psyol river. Yury Dolgoruky force
1 CONC d him to flee to Poland in 1155, but the next year Mstislav returned with a new army and defeated Dolgoruky at Volodymyr-Volynsky. Dolgoruky died in 1157, and Mstislav had himself crowned at Volodymyr-Volynsky.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1151 Mstislav married Agnieszka, the daughter of King Boleslaus III of Poland. They had three sons:
1 CONT
1 CONT Roman Mstislavich (c. 1152-1205) 
1 CONT Sviatoslav Mstislavich, Prince of Brest 
1 CONT Vsevolod Mstislavich of Volhynia, Prince of Belz, Prince of Volodymyr-Volynsky (died 1196) 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Iziaslav III Grand Prince of Kiev Succeeded by:
1 CONT Gleb I 
