0 @N6000000002188005012@ NOTE George I of Halych
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Yuriy I of Halych also Yuriy I of Lviv (born April 24 1252 (1257 ?) — March 18, 1308) - Prince of Belz (1264-1301), king of Halych-Volhynia (1301-1308).
1 CONT
1 CONT He was a son of Lev Danylovich (Knyaz of Halych, 1269 — 1301) and Constance of Hungary, a daughter of King Béla IV. His father was a son of Danylo of Halych
1 CONT
1 CONT He married three times. His first wife was Yaroslavna of Tver (died ca. 1286). His second wife was Euphemia of Kuyavia (died 18 March 1308), daughter of Prince Konrad of Masovia, Kuyavia, Leczyca, and Sieradz.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Family
1 CONT Sons
1 CONT
1 CONT Michail (1283 - 1286) (first marriage) 
1 CONT Andriy, King of Halych-Volhynia (1308-23) 
1 CONT Lev II, Prince of Lutsk (1308-23) 
1 CONT Daughters
1 CONT
1 CONT Eufemia, Princess of Volynia-Lutsk (married Lubart Gediminovich of Lithuania (dead 1384)) 
1 CONT Maria, Princess of Halych-Lviv, (died 11 January 1341). Married Trojden I of Masovia 
1 CONT Anastasia (parentage uncertain) (died 1364-65). Married Alexander I of Tver (who died 28 October 1339) 
1 CONT [edit]
